<title>ITALY: Mini-budget keeps Italy on course for EMU - Prodi.</title>
<headline>Mini-budget keeps Italy on course for EMU - Prodi.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi said a mini-budget approved on Thursday would help Italy meet the terms of the Maastricht Treaty.</p>
<p>&quot;The government has approved a corrective budget that will enable us to meet the parameters,&quot; Prodi told a news conference after the cabinet had approved the package.</p>
<p>Prodi said the mini-budget included 15.5 trillion lire of deficit cuts needed to plug a hole in Italy's state accounts and keep Italy on course to join the single currency from its planned launch in 1999. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
